       expands from 0 to 2.781615E+5 eV, with resonance           3925 1451   25
       extracted from the "radiator" TARES database. A total of   3925 1451   26
       3 l-values are used and 335 resonances. The resonance      3925 1451   27
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              3925 1451   28
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       3925 1451   29
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          3925 1451   30
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     3925 1451   31
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    3925 1451   32
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  3925 1451   33
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   3925 1451   34
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          3925 1451   35
